#!/bin/sh
# PATH shim routing claude at the work or personal config dir, mirroring
# ~/bin/pi. A script rather than a shell function because functions only exist
# in interactive shells, and agent-spawned invocations are the ones that most
# need routing.

real_claude=/opt/homebrew/bin/claude

if [ ! -x "$real_claude" ]; then
	echo "claude shim: $real_claude is missing or not executable" >&2
	exit 127
fi

# An explicitly set value is a stated intention and outranks the path rule, so
# a nested claude keeps its parent session's account even when the worktree it
# runs in sits outside the parent's tree.
if [ -z "$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR" ]; then
	# Absolute path: the shim may be invoked from a context whose PATH does not
	# carry ~/bin.
	if [ "$("$HOME/bin/agent-account")" = personal ]; then
		CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR="$HOME/.claude-personal"
		export CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
	fi
fi

# Absolute path so the shim cannot re-invoke itself through PATH.
exec "$real_claude" "$@"
